\subsection*{Decentralized Monetization Models}

\begin{enumerate}
    \setcounter{enumi}{45}
    \item \textbf{Gogel, D., et al. (2021)}. DeFi Beyond the Hype: The Emerging World of Decentralized Finance. \url{https://wifpr.wharton.upenn.edu/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/DeFi-Beyond-the-Hype.pdf}
    
    \textbf{Annotation:} The purpose of this report is to explain the concept of DeFi, outlining its main features, the architecture of the DeFi ecosystem, and prospective developments.

    \item \textbf{Khan, K. (2024)}. Decentralized Video Streaming: Unleashing the Potential through Blockchain-Powered Platforms. \url{http://ijmrap.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/IJMRAP-V6N7P97Y23.pdf}
    
    \textbf{Annotation:} This paper examines the paradigm shift toward decentralized video platforms, driven by blockchain technology. It assesses the core principles of decentralized video streaming, highlighting the potential benefits for content creators, users, and the broader streaming ecosystem.

    \item \textbf{Gomaa, A. (2019)}. A DRM Solution for Online Content Using Blockchain - A Music Perspective. \url{https://personales.upv.es/thinkmind/dl/conferences/infocomp/infocomp_2019/infocomp_2019_1_30_60048.pdf}
    
    \textbf{Annotation:} This document proposes a DRM framework to monetize, monitor, and regulate digital content across platforms. It aims to reduce entry barriers for musical groups, facilitate royalty distributions, and control content dissemination. The paper leverages recent advancements in blockchain and cryptocurrency.

    \item \textbf{Castweet Team. (2019)}. Castweet - A Multi-broadcast Platform Based on Blockchain Incentives for Everyone. \url{https://resources.cryptocompare.com/asset-management/17402/1728919640132.pdf}
    
    \textbf{Annotation:} This paper reviews the Castweet Ecosystem, which promotes sustainable engagement by showcasing use cases for viewers and creators. Many blockchain incentive systems focus on rewards, enabling earning but neglecting genuine token use cases.

    \item \textbf{Banerjee, P., et al. (2020)}. Reliable, Fair and Decentralized Marketplace for Content Sharing Using Blockchain. \url{https://arxiv.org/pdf/2009.11033}
    
    \textbf{Annotation:} This paper proposes a dependable and equitable platform for content sharing that functions without a central intermediary. The platform is designed as a decentralized data storage layer aimed at securely storing and distributing content in a fault-tolerant manner, with peers also participating within a blockchain network.

    \item \textbf{Munson, M. (2019)}. A Blockchain Controlled Content Fabric. \url{https://static.vsf.tv/Meetings/2019/2019_DC/Munson_BlockchainFabric.pdf}
    
